# Supply-chain hardening: 7-day release cooldown.
#
# Only versions that have been on the registry for more than 7 days are eligible
# for installation. This blunts the "publish malicious version -> get pulled into
# CI within minutes" class of attack (Shai-Hulud et al.), which relies on fast
# automated consumption before the version is detected and unpublished.
#
# !! REQUIRES npm >= 11.10.0 !!
# `min-release-age` was added in npm 11.10.0 (2026-02-11). Older npm silently
# IGNORES unknown .npmrc keys - it does not warn and it does not fail. On npm
# 10.x this file provides NO protection whatsoever.
#
# This file is NOT published (it is not in package.json's `files` allowlist), so
# it applies to this repo's own dev installs and to CI only - it has no effect on
# consumers of @startupkit-app/jobs. CI must pin npm >= 11.10.0 (e.g.
# `npm i -g npm@^11.10.0`, or actions/setup-node with a matching npm) or the
# cooldown is not applied there either.
#
# Unit is DAYS (npm). Note pnpm's equivalent `minimumReleaseAge` is in MINUTES -
# do not copy this value across package managers without converting.
min-release-age=7
